   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Large tropical black Asian forest scorpion (Heterometrus spinifer) sp. Kumai, Kalimantan, Indonesia, Borneo. The exoskeletal skin of many scorpions takes on an unusual property as it hardens; it fluoresces brightly under ultraviolet light. This individual</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
